title: check re-applies the manifest after config load, undoing `defines` removals (B024 follow-up)
updated_at: "2026-08-29T07:02:27Z"
---
Found 2026-08-29 while planning the signature-mode work. Regression window:
introduced by B024 (custom defines became additive with `-NAME` removals).

## Symptom
CLI `check` and the LSP server disagree about `-NAME` removals of a
MANIFEST-derived define. Repro:

    info.toml            [script] defines = ["MANIFEST_OFF"]
    .openplanet-lsp.toml defines = ["-MANIFEST_OFF"]
    src/Main.as          #if MANIFEST_OFF
                         MissingType removal_was_undone;
                         #endif

`check --no-typedb` reports 2 errors — the branch is live. `LspConfig::load`
alone (the LSP path) drops MANIFEST_OFF correctly; the unit test
`config_defines_apply_after_manifest_defines` passes.

## Cause
src/cli/mod.rs `run_check` calls `LspConfig::load(Some(&root), None)`, which
already applies the plugin manifest at Layer 4 and the user's define
overrides at Layer 5. `run_check` then loads `root/info.toml` and calls
`config.apply_manifest(&manifest)` a SECOND time, re-inserting every
manifest/dependency define AFTER the removals ran.

The second call is redundant even without B024 — `load` covers the same root.

## Fix
Drop the duplicate `apply_manifest` block in `run_check`. Keep one seam:
`LspConfig::load` owns the whole ladder.

## Test plan (TDD, red first)
Red: the fixture above via the `check` subprocess must report 0 diagnostics.
Variants: `-DEPENDENCY_X` removal of a dependency-derived define; a manifest
define NOT removed still survives (guards over-deletion); the LSP path keeps
agreeing (existing unit test); `--define MANIFEST_OFF` on the command line
still wins over a config `-MANIFEST_OFF` (CLI flag is the top layer).